 and then tot, and I'll start that at 0.0.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:15.240
 So that's the running count and the running total.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.440
 Now we need to write a loop,

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.000
 and I'm going to write this as an infinite loop,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.720
 while true, with colon, and then I'll indent,

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.760
 and I'll prompt for a string, and remember, input

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.280
 gives us a string, so I'm going to call this sval

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.280
 equals input, enter a number, colon, space.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:46.600
 I'm going to deal with the try and accept later,

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.460
 but you can just kind of know that the floating point value

