 sval, this input returns us a string,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.520
 and now I'm going to convert that to float.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:11.920
 I'm going to say print fval, so I can print that out,

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:18.760
 and then I'm going to do the num equals num,

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.120
 plus one, and tot equals tot plus fval.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:35.880
 Now, I do need to deal with the situation

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.680
 where I'm entering the word done.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.560
 Now, we want to check that before we convert it to a float,

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.120
 because done, well, we can run this.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.960
 It's an infinite loop, but it'll only run a little bit,

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.760
 won't cause us too much problem.

